     There were other problems besides that.  When trapped, you could
escape the web by simply traversing the stairs.  Conversely, returning
to that level via the stairs wouldn't even check to see whether you
should become trapped.  Those problems could have been fixed separately,
but this change was both easier and more consistent with the handling
of other player settable traps.  And the display issue is significant;
tiles may conceivably be able to simultaneously show both a trap and
a dungeon feature at the same location, but simple ASCII can't (unless
you want to devote some scarce unused character to mean `you'd better
look more closely here...').


